;;;
;;; curator.theory — the dashboard's own mind-shaped process.
;;;
;;; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
;;;
;;;   IT RECORDS.  IT DOES NOT CONCLUDE.
;;;
;;;   That sentence is the whole design, and everything below follows
;;;   from it.  The Curator holds RELATIONS and answers TUPLES.  It
;;;   has no Totality of thought: no schemes, no activation, no
;;;   reasoning, no reifiers.  A dashboard that inferred things would
;;;   be a second mind with a worse view than the first, and the two
;;;   would eventually disagree about a learner they both watch.
;;;
;;;   Keeping it in a separate process makes that boundary STRUCTURAL
;;;   rather than a rule somebody has to remember.
;;;
;;; ── WHY IT EXISTS AT ALL ─────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;;   Three things the dashboard knows that no learner can:
;;;
;;;   WHAT IT ITSELF SENT.  The dashboard is a sender in three places
;;;   — the Attempts composer, the Signals screen, the Competency
;;;   toggle.  Without a record of those, THE ARCHIVE CANNOT TELL AN
;;;   ATTEMPT THE MIND DECIDED FROM ONE A PERSON TYPED, and this
;;;   entire project rests on evidence being auditable.  That is the
;;;   first reason and the strongest.
;;;
;;;   WHAT IT ASKED.  A signal case is a stimulus, an expectation and
;;;   a deadline.  A mind should not keep a record of having been
;;;   probed; the prober should.
;;;
;;;   WHAT IT SAW ACROSS LEARNERS.  Cost per win, frontier burn-down,
;;;   assimilation ratio — compared across runs and across minds,
;;;   which is exactly what no single mind can hold.
;;;
;;;   And one it knows about minds that are DOWN.  A learner that has
;;;   fallen over cannot write down that it fell over.
;;;
;;; ── WHAT IT MUST NEVER HOLD ──────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;;   Anything derived from a learner's Totality.  Cases, activations,
;;;   schemes, remindings, canvases — those are read through that
;;;   learner's own portal.theory and NEVER COPIED HERE.  A second
;;;   reader with its own scoring is the failure this tree keeps
;;;   finding; a second COPY is the same failure with a delay on it.
;;;
;;;   Competency profiles are not here either.  A competency is a
;;;   design pattern in a particular mind, and two learners may not
;;;   have the same ones.  Profiles belong in the learner's Totality.
;;;
;;; ── THE HANDSHAKE, ONE LEVEL UP ──────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;;   A psyche announces itself to a mind's Registrar and is granted a
;;;   token and the addresses it should speak on.  A LEARNER
;;;   announces itself HERE and is granted its place in the roster.
;;;
;;;     Psyche  -> Registrar   [REGISTER :Psyche  …] -> [PSYCHE  …]
;;;     Learner -> Curator     [ENROLL   :Learner …] -> [ENROLLED …]
;;;
;;;   Same shape, same one door, same doctrine that the grant tells
;;;   the asker what it needs.  That the existing mechanism fits
;;;   unaltered is the strongest evidence the layering is right.
;;;
;;;   ANNOUNCING IS BEST-EFFORT.  A learner announces and carries on
;;;   whether or not anything answers — as Eidos retries.  So a
;;;   headless run needs no dashboard at all, and a dashboard started
;;;   later picks learners up on their next heartbeat.
;;;
;;; ── WHAT IS LOST ON RESTART DEPENDS ON THE ADAPTER ───────────────
;;;
;;;   [Curator :Adapter] is configured, not decided here.  On
;;;   ephemeral-kb the roster and the injections go when the process
;;;   does; on a durable adapter they do not.  THE SCREENS MUST SAY
;;;   WHICH, because an injections record that silently starts empty
;;;   looks like a dashboard that has sent nothing — a claim about
;;;   the mind rather than about the adapter.
;;;
;;; *************************************************************************************

(theory Curator {1 0 0}

  "Curator — what the dashboard has observed, and what it sent."


  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ;;; §1  THE ROSTER
  ;;;
  ;;; WHO EXISTS, AND WHAT IT TAKES TO START ONE.
  ;;;
  ;;; Three kinds of knowledge about a learner, and only one of them
  ;;; is durable:
  ;;;
  ;;;   CONFIGURED   id, name, home, being, record — what it takes to
  ;;;                START one.  Must persist outside every mind,
  ;;;                because A STOPPED LEARNER CANNOT ANSWER.
  ;;;
  ;;;   GRANTED      perceiver, executor, token — arrives in the
  ;;;                PSYCHE grant.  Discovered, never stored.
  ;;;
  ;;;   OBSERVED     running, attached to — true only while running.
  ;;;                Asked, never stored.
  ;;;
  ;;; Storing the second or third would be the Device :Status failure
  ;;; over again: a copy going stale while the truth moves.
  ;;;
  ;;; :Seen IS THE ONE VOLATILE SLOT, and it earns its place.
  ;;; Liveness cannot be ASKED of something that is down, and "when
  ;;; did anyone last hear from this" is exactly what an operator
  ;;; needs to know about a learner that is not answering.
  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  (relation Learner
    :Id        nil     ; what everything names it by
    :Name      ""      ; what an operator reads
    :Home      ""      ; to start it
    :Being     ""      ; to start it
    :Record    ""      ; where its messages land
    :Registrar ""      ; its own Registrar — the one configured url
    :Totality  ""      ; for display: what it is attached to
    :Born      0       ; first enrolment
    :Seen      0       ; last heartbeat
  )


  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ;;; §2  PSYCHES
  ;;;
  ;;; Which devices which learner has admitted.
  ;;;
  ;;; THE LEARNER KNOWS THIS ALREADY — its Registrar minted a Device
  ;;; row.  What is kept here is the CROSS-LEARNER view: two learners
  ;;; on one Eidos, a psyche that registered with the wrong mind, a
  ;;; device answering nobody.  None of those is visible from inside
  ;;; any single mind.
  ;;;
  ;;; And it survives the learner.  A mind that has fallen over takes
  ;;; its Device rows with it, and the question afterwards is usually
  ;;; what it had been talking to.
  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  (relation Psyche
    :Learner   nil     ; whose
    :Name      nil     ; Eidos, Expanse
    :Address   ""      ; its door
    :Channels  {}      ; what it offers
    :Seen      0       ; last tuple observed from it
  )


  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ;;; §3  INJECTIONS
  ;;;
  ;;; EVERY TUPLE THE DASHBOARD ITSELF SENT.
  ;;;
  ;;; THIS IS THE FIRST REASON THE CURATOR EXISTS.  The portal is a
  ;;; viewer everywhere and a sender in exactly three places: the
  ;;; Attempts composer, the Signals screen, the Competency toggle.
  ;;;
  ;;; Without this record the archive cannot distinguish an attempt
  ;;; the mind DECIDED from one a person TYPED — and a campaign whose
  ;;; evidence cannot be told apart from its operator's interference
  ;;; is a campaign that proves nothing.  Forty-five live runs are
  ;;; worth what they are worth because nobody was helping.
  ;;;
  ;;; RECORDED WHETHER IT SUCCEEDED OR NOT.  A tuple that failed to
  ;;; send still tells you what somebody tried, and a refusal is
  ;;; evidence about the gate rather than absence of evidence.
  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  (relation Injection
    :Learner   nil     ; to which mind
    :Head      nil     ; ATTEMPT, PERCEPT, COMPETENCY, PSYCHE …
    :Tuple     ""      ; verbatim, as sent
    :Whom      ""      ; where it went
    :Answer    ""      ; what came back, or the error
    :Screen    nil     ; which screen sent it
    :Moment    0
  )


  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ;;; §4  SIGNAL CASES
  ;;;
  ;;; A stimulus, an expectation, a deadline, and what happened.
  ;;;
  ;;; THE PROBER KEEPS THE RECORD, NOT THE PROBED.  A mind has no
  ;;; business holding an account of having been experimented on —
  ;;; it would be evidence about the experimenter sitting in the
  ;;; evidence about the mind.
  ;;;
  ;;; :Met is three-valued on purpose.  `waiting` is not `missed`:
  ;;; a case still within its deadline has not failed, and collapsing
  ;;; the two would make every case that is merely slow look like a
  ;;; case that went wrong.
  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  (relation Signal
    :Learner   nil     ; which mind was probed
    :Sent      ""      ; the afferent tuple, verbatim
    :Expect    nil     ; ATTEMPT | RESULT
    :Match     ""      ; the slot expression that had to match
    :Deadline  0       ; how long, in its units
    :Units     beats   ; beats | moments
    :Met       waiting ; waiting | met | missed
    :Got       ""      ; the answering tuple, where one came
    :Latency   0       ; how long it took
    :Moment    0
  )


  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ;;; §5  RUNS
  ;;;
  ;;; One bounded episode per learner — which world, when it opened,
  ;;; how it ended.
  ;;;
  ;;; THE LEDGER ALREADY EXISTS, one line per run, on each learner's
  ;;; own disk.  This is the INDEX ACROSS THEM: the same campaign run
  ;;; by two learners, or by one learner before and after a
  ;;; competency was spun up, is a comparison neither learner's ledger
  ;;; can make.
  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  (relation Run
    :Learner   nil
    :World     nil     ; the channel — ls20-9607e27b
    :Opened    0
    :Closed    0
    :Levels    0       ; how far it got
    :Actions   0       ; what it spent
    :Outcome   nil     ; attained | terminated | abandoned | running
    :Profile   ""      ; which competencies were up, by name
  )


  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ;;; §6  MEASURES
  ;;;
  ;;; Derived per run; compared across runs and across learners.
  ;;;
  ;;; THE NUMBERS THAT MAKE THE CLAIM MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED —
  ;;; cost per win, frontier burn-down, assimilation ratio,
  ;;; exploration rate, model confirmation.  μ-GIL's curves exist;
  ;;; recomputing them for GIL is what turns "it works" into a result.
  ;;;
  ;;; ONE ROW PER MEASURE PER RUN, rather than a wide row of every
  ;;; measure, because the set of measures will grow and a wide row
  ;;; would have to be altered every time it did.
  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  (relation Measure
    :Run       nil
    :Learner   nil
    :Name      nil     ; cost-per-win, frontier, assimilation …
    :Value     0.0
    :At        0       ; the decision or run index it was taken at
  )


  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ;;; §7  NOTICES
  ;;;
  ;;; The dashboard's own observations about health.
  ;;;
  ;;; A LEARNER THAT HAS FALLEN OVER CANNOT WRITE DOWN THAT IT FELL
  ;;; OVER.  Nothing else records a mind that stopped answering, a
  ;;; build that failed, an audit that came back dirty — and those
  ;;; are precisely the facts wanted afterwards, when the thing that
  ;;; would have recorded them is the thing that is gone.
  ;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  (relation Notice
    :Learner   nil     ; whom it concerns, or nil for the dashboard
    :Kind      nil     ; silent | build-failed | audit-dirty | enrolled …
    :Detail    ""
    :Moment    0
  )


  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ;;; §8  ENROLMENT — the handshake
  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  (function enroll {?t}
    "Absorb [ENROLL :Learner … ] and answer [ENROLLED …].

     UPDATES, IT DOES NOT DUPLICATE.  A learner restarting announces
     itself again; a second row would leave the first holding a
     :Seen that nothing will ever advance, and an operator looking at
     two rows for one mind.

     :Born SURVIVES.  When the mind was first seen is a different
     fact from when it was last seen, and restarting does not make it
     new."
    (var ?id (:Learner ?t))
    (if (null-p ?id)
        [ENROLLED :Status Refused :Reason "no :Learner slot"]
        (do
          (var ?row (with [Learner :Id = ?id] give ?me))
          (if (null-p ?row)
              (do
                (new Learner
                  :Id        ?id
                  :Name      (default (:Name ?t) (string ?id))
                  :Home      (default (:Home ?t) "")
                  :Being     (default (:Being ?t) "")
                  :Record    (default (:Record ?t) "")
                  :Registrar (default (:Registrar ?t) "")
                  :Totality  (default (:Totality ?t) "")
                  :Born      (moment)
                  :Seen      (moment))
                (notice ?id enrolled ($ "first seen: " ?id)))
              (put ?row
                :Name      (default (:Name ?t) (:Name ?row))
                :Home      (default (:Home ?t) (:Home ?row))
                :Being     (default (:Being ?t) (:Being ?row))
                :Record    (default (:Record ?t) (:Record ?row))
                :Registrar (default (:Registrar ?t) (:Registrar ?row))
                :Totality  (default (:Totality ?t) (:Totality ?row))
                :Seen      (moment)))
          [ENROLLED :Status Granted :Learner ?id :Moment (moment)])))


  (function heartbeat {?t}
    "A learner saying it is still there.

     Cheaper than an enrolment and carrying nothing but the fact.
     A learner whose :Seen has stopped advancing is a learner that
     has stopped — which is the one thing it cannot tell anybody
     itself."
    (var ?id (:Learner ?t))
    (with [Learner :Id = ?id] as ?row
      do (put ?row :Seen (moment)))
    [BEAT :Learner ?id :Moment (moment)])


  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ;;; §9  RECORDING
  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  (function record-injection {?t}
    "Write down a tuple the dashboard sent.

     WHETHER OR NOT IT SUCCEEDED.  A tuple that failed to send still
     tells you what somebody tried, and a refusal is evidence about
     the gate rather than an absence of evidence."
    (new Injection
      :Learner (:Learner ?t)
      :Head    (:Head ?t)
      :Tuple   (default (:Tuple ?t) "")
      :Whom    (default (:Whom ?t) "")
      :Answer  (default (:Answer ?t) "")
      :Screen  (default (:Screen ?t) unknown)
      :Moment  (moment))
    [RECORDED :Of Injection :Moment (moment)])


  (function record-signal {?t}
    "Open or settle a signal case.

     OPENED WHEN SENT, SETTLED WHEN ANSWERED — one row, twice
     written, rather than two rows to be paired up afterwards.  A
     case that is never settled stays `waiting`, which is the honest
     record of a probe whose answer never came."
    (var ?open (with [Signal :Learner = (:Learner ?t) :Met = waiting] give ?me))
    (if (and (thing-p ?open) (thing-p (:Got ?t)))
        (do
          (put ?open
            :Met     (default (:Met ?t) met)
            :Got     (default (:Got ?t) "")
            :Latency (default (:Latency ?t) 0))
          [RECORDED :Of Signal :Status (:Met ?open)])
        (do
          (new Signal
            :Learner  (:Learner ?t)
            :Sent     (default (:Sent ?t) "")
            :Expect   (:Expect ?t)
            :Match    (default (:Match ?t) "")
            :Deadline (default (:Deadline ?t) 0)
            :Units    (default (:Units ?t) beats)
            :Met      waiting
            :Moment   (moment))
          [RECORDED :Of Signal :Status waiting])))


  (function notice {?learner literal ?kind string ?detail}
    "Write down something the dashboard observed."
    (new Notice :Learner ?learner :Kind ?kind
                :Detail ?detail :Moment (moment))
    ?kind)


  (function curator-ask {?t}
    "Answer a question about what is known.

     A ROW, NOT A FEED.  The feeds are for screens, which poll and
     want everything; this is for a mechanism that wants one thing
     and wants it now — spawn-learner asking where a learner lives,
     because the roster is the dashboard\'s and a learner has no
     business keeping one.

     AN UNKNOWN LEARNER IS ANSWERED, NOT IGNORED.  Nothing here
     means nothing is known, and a caller told so can say which
     learner it was asked about — where silence would leave it
     guessing whether the Curator was down."
    (case (:Of ?t)
      of Learner
        (with [Learner :Id = (:Id ?t) :Name as ?n :Home as ?h
                       :Being as ?b :Record as ?rec :Registrar as ?reg
                       :Totality as ?tot :Born as ?born :Seen as ?seen]
          give [LEARNER :Id (:Id ?t) :Name ?n :Home ?h :Being ?b
                        :Record ?rec :Registrar ?reg :Totality ?tot
                        :Born ?born :Seen ?seen]
          else [LEARNER :Id (:Id ?t) :Status Unknown])
      else
        [ANSWER :Of (:Of ?t) :Status Unknown]))


  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ;;; §10  THE SILENCE WATCH
  ;;;
  ;;; A learner whose :Seen has stopped advancing has stopped.
  ;;;
  ;;; NOTICED ONCE, NOT EVERY PASS.  A notice per cycle for a mind
  ;;; that is down would bury every other notice within a minute —
  ;;; and the fact worth recording is that it WENT silent, which
  ;;; happens once, not that it IS silent, which is a query.
  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  (agent Curator
    (function {}
      (when (cancelled-p (self)) (exit yes))
      (var ?now  (moment))
      (var ?wait (setting Curator Curator :Silence))
      (with [Learner :Id as ?id :Seen as ?seen]
            (and (> ?seen 0) (> (- ?now ?seen) ?wait))
        do
        (unless (with [Notice :Learner = ?id :Kind = silent] give yes)
          (notice ?id silent ($ "no heartbeat since " ?seen)))))

    (setting Curator Curator :Url)

    ;;; ── THE ONE DOOR ────────────────────────────────────────────
    ;;;
    ;;; Same doctrine as everywhere else: one address, one handler,
    ;;; routed by the tuple's head.  A learner enrolling, a dashboard
    ;;; recording what it sent, and a screen asking what is known all
    ;;; arrive the same way.
    (function {?sender ?message}
      (var ?t (parse ?message))
      (case (top ?t)
        of ENROLL    (tell ?sender ($ (enroll ?t)))
        of BEAT      (tell ?sender ($ (heartbeat ?t)))
        of INJECTED  (tell ?sender ($ (record-injection ?t)))
        of SIGNALLED (tell ?sender ($ (record-signal ?t)))
        of NOTICE    (tell ?sender
                       ($ [RECORDED :Of Notice
                                    :Kind (notice (:Learner ?t) (:Kind ?t)
                                                  (default (:Detail ?t) ""))]))
        of ASK       (tell ?sender ($ (curator-ask ?t)))
        of WATCHING  (do (curator-watching (:Screen ?t))
                         (tell ?sender ($ [WATCHED :Screen (:Screen ?t)])))
        else
          (trace ($ "[Curator] unknown tuple: " (top ?t)))))

    (setting Curator Curator :Delay)
    {curating})


  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ;;; §11  THE FEEDS
  ;;;
  ;;; Written the same way portal.theory writes a learner's, and to
  ;;; the same folder, so the dashboard polls one place for both.
  ;;;
  ;;; THE PREFIX SAYS WHOSE.  A learner's feeds are portal-*.json and
  ;;; the dashboard's are curator-*.json, because a screen showing a
  ;;; learner's percepts beside the dashboard's own record must never
  ;;; leave a reader guessing which is which.
  ;;;
  ;;; AND EVERY FEED CARRIES THE ADAPTER.  What is lost on restart
  ;;; depends on it, and an injections list that silently starts
  ;;; empty looks like a dashboard that has sent nothing — a claim
  ;;; about the mind rather than about the configuration.
  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  (var ?*CURATOR-SCREEN* none)

  (function curator-watching {literal ?screen}
    (set ?*CURATOR-SCREEN* ?screen)
    ?screen)


  (function curator-path {literal ?name}
    ($$ (setting Curator Curator :Log) "curator-" (string ?name) ".json"))


  (function curator-write {literal ?name string ?json}
    "Atomically — the dashboard polls these and parses whatever it
     finds the moment it appears."
    (var ?path (curator-path ?name))
    (var ?tmp  ($$ ?path ".tmp"))
    (var ?f    (file ?tmp))
    (write ?f ?json)
    (close ?f)
    (move ?tmp ?path)
    ?path)


  (function c-str {?v}  ($$ "\"" (string ?v) "\""))
  (function c-num {?v}  (string ?v))
  (function c-pair {literal ?k string ?v} ($$ "\"" (string ?k) "\":" ?v))
  (function c-object {list ?ps} ($$ "{" (join ?ps ",") "}"))
  (function c-array {list ?is}  ($$ "[" (join ?is ",") "]"))


  (function curator-learners {}
    (var ?rows {})
    (with [Learner :Id as ?id :Name as ?n :Home as ?h :Being as ?b
                   :Record as ?rec :Registrar as ?reg :Totality as ?tot
                   :Born as ?born :Seen as ?seen]
      do
      (set ?rows (adjoin ?rows
        (c-object {(c-pair id        (c-str ?id))
                   (c-pair name      (c-str ?n))
                   (c-pair home      (c-str ?h))
                   (c-pair being     (c-str ?b))
                   (c-pair record    (c-str ?rec))
                   (c-pair registrar (c-str ?reg))
                   (c-pair totality  (c-str ?tot))
                   (c-pair born      (c-str ?born))
                   (c-pair seen      (c-str ?seen))}))))
    (curator-write learners
      (c-object {(c-pair adapter  (c-str (setting Curator Curator :Adapter)))
                 (c-pair learners (c-array ?rows))})))


  (function curator-injections {}
    (var ?rows {})
    (var ?cap (default (setting Curator Curator :History) 200))
    (with [Injection :Learner as ?l :Head as ?h :Tuple as ?t
                     :Whom as ?w :Answer as ?a :Screen as ?s :Moment as ?at]
          sort ?cap
      do
      (set ?rows (adjoin ?rows
        (c-object {(c-pair learner (c-str ?l))
                   (c-pair head    (c-str ?h))
                   (c-pair tuple   (c-str ?t))
                   (c-pair whom    (c-str ?w))
                   (c-pair answer  (c-str ?a))
                   (c-pair screen  (c-str ?s))
                   (c-pair moment  (c-str ?at))}))))
    (curator-write injections
      (c-object {(c-pair adapter (c-str (setting Curator Curator :Adapter)))
                 (c-pair rows    (c-array ?rows))})))


  (function curator-signals {}
    (var ?rows {})
    (with [Signal :Learner as ?l :Sent as ?s :Expect as ?e :Match as ?m
                  :Deadline as ?d :Units as ?u :Met as ?met :Got as ?g
                  :Latency as ?lat :Moment as ?at]
      do
      (set ?rows (adjoin ?rows
        (c-object {(c-pair learner  (c-str ?l))
                   (c-pair sent     (c-str ?s))
                   (c-pair expect   (c-str ?e))
                   (c-pair match    (c-str ?m))
                   (c-pair deadline (c-num ?d))
                   (c-pair units    (c-str ?u))
                   (c-pair met      (c-str ?met))
                   (c-pair got      (c-str ?g))
                   (c-pair latency  (c-num ?lat))
                   (c-pair moment   (c-str ?at))}))))
    (curator-write signals (c-array ?rows)))


  (function curator-notices {}
    (var ?rows {})
    (with [Notice :Learner as ?l :Kind as ?k :Detail as ?d :Moment as ?at]
      do
      (set ?rows (adjoin ?rows
        (c-object {(c-pair learner (c-str ?l))
                   (c-pair kind    (c-str ?k))
                   (c-pair detail  (c-str ?d))
                   (c-pair moment  (c-str ?at))}))))
    (curator-write notices (c-array ?rows)))


  (function curator-runs {}
    (var ?rows {})
    (with [Run :Learner as ?l :World as ?w :Opened as ?o :Closed as ?c
               :Levels as ?lv :Actions as ?a :Outcome as ?out
               :Profile as ?prof]
      do
      (set ?rows (adjoin ?rows
        (c-object {(c-pair learner (c-str ?l))
                   (c-pair world   (c-str ?w))
                   (c-pair opened  (c-str ?o))
                   (c-pair closed  (c-str ?c))
                   (c-pair levels  (c-num ?lv))
                   (c-pair actions (c-num ?a))
                   (c-pair outcome (c-str ?out))
                   (c-pair profile (c-str ?prof))}))))
    (curator-write runs (c-array ?rows)))


  (function curator-pass {}
    "Write the feed for whatever is being watched.

     The roster goes every pass regardless, because the Learner
     screen is not the only one that needs to know which mind is
     answering — every other screen is about a particular learner
     and none of them should have to ask twice."
    (curator-learners)
    (case ?*CURATOR-SCREEN*
      of learner    (curator-notices)
      of signals    (curator-signals)
      of attempts   (curator-injections)
      of runs       (do (curator-runs) (curator-injections))
      else          nil))


  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ;;; §12  START
  ;;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  (function curate {}
    "Open the dashboard's knowledge base and start the Curator.

     ITS OWN KB, AT ITS OWN URL, WITH ITS OWN ADAPTER.  Not any
     learner's Totality: learner A's cannot be the registry for B
     without making A special, and A being down would hide B.
     Whether it is memory or a database is the deployment's business
     and is read from the registry."
    (use (lore url (setting Curator Curator :Kb)
                   adapter (setting Curator Curator :Adapter))
      (start Curator)
      (trace ($ "[Curator] " (setting Curator Curator :Adapter)
                " at " (setting Curator Curator :Kb)))
      curating))


) ;; end theory Curator

;; ---------------  end of file -----------------
